  "label": "kitten is the subject of the text",
  "description": "The text 'when your kitten can't find a box' explicitly refers to the kitten in the image as the subject of the scenario. The visual material (the kitten in the box) is mapped onto the textual entity 'kitten' to create the analogy that the kitten is experiencing the situation described in the text. This is a direct analogical mapping where the visual entity (kitten) is identified as the entity referred to by the text.",
